#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:206
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "\"Flake\" is not a root cause. A red PR is work now, whatever its review state — only a green, mergeable head waits on reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:244
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`prepare-merge` brings the base in, re-runs the gates and pushes — it does NOT merge. Bringing the base in IS `merge-base.bpmn` (`bun run cat merge:main`): conflicts a declared pattern covers are resolved and proved by the gate set; anything else aborts the merge and comes back to the agent (bean `y7b3`, #1707). `watch` follows the PR until it is merged or closed, because webhooks do not reliably deliver CI success or a merge-conflict transition."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:261
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A closed work item is read later by somebody deciding whether to reopen the subject, so \"completed\" with nothing behind it cannot be audited. An ISSUE is never closed on the agent's own say-so."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:301
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A human or an agent acting AS reviewer. Nothing is a reviewer; somebody acts as one for the duration of this lane. For a rendered change the reviewer reads the agent's before/after preview rather than building one. On agent-touched changes, an adversarial code review evaluates against the RED FLAG taxonomy and writes a committed verdict."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "A platform change is needed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:224
#. Diagram label
msgid "Address the review"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:135
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Announce the branch WHEN IT IS CREATED, not when the work is done. The gap between one agent's view of an issue and everyone else's is what this closes."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn:199
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the gates run against the merge of head into base. `green` goes to review; `red` goes to root-causing the failure first, since a red change is never waiting on review."
msgstr ""

